#pagebreak(weak: true)
#align(center, text(size: 7pt, tracking: 0.12em)[QUESTIONS FOR REFLECTION])
#v(0.1in)

#set enum(spacing: 0.9em, indent: 0pt, body-indent: 0.6em)

+ Pascal says our unhappiness comes from not being able to stay quietly in a
  room. When did you last sit for ten minutes with nothing to look at? What
  happened?

+ The gambler does not want the money as a gift, and he is bored playing for
  nothing (139). What is the "chase" you enjoy more than the "quarry"?

+ Who plays the courtiers around the king today, making sure we are never
  "alone and in a state to think of ourselves" (142)?

+ "The present is never our end" (172). Where does your attention live: in
  the past, the future, or here?

+ Fragment 171 calls diversion both our only consolation and our greatest
  misery. How can both be true?

+ Pascal's answer is not "no more games" but a heart filled by the right
  object (425). What would it mean for your attention to rest there?

#pagebreak()
#align(center, text(size: 7pt, tracking: 0.12em)[A SHORT GLOSSARY])
#v(0.1in)
#set par(justify: false, spacing: 0.75em)
#text(size: 7.8pt)[
*Diversion* (_divertissement_). Literally a turning aside: whatever turns our
mind away from our own condition.

*Weariness* (_ennui_). The flat, heavy boredom that rises when diversion stops.

*Chamber.* A private room. Pascal's "stay quietly in their own chamber" is the
line usually quoted as "sit quietly in a room."

*Court tennis.* The ball "caught in its fall from the roof" (140) is from the
indoor game of _jeu de paume_, played off sloping roofs around the court.

*Pyrrhus.* King of Epirus. His adviser asked what he would do after conquering
Italy, Sicily and Africa. "Rest and enjoy ourselves." Then why not rest now?

*Superintendent, chancellor, first president.* The great offices of the
French crown.

*In omnibus requiem quaesivi.* "In all things I sought rest" (Ecclesiasticus
24:11).

*Memoria hospitis unius diei praetereuntis.* "The remembrance of a guest that
tarrieth but a day" (Wisdom 5:15).
]
#set par(justify: true)
